            "type": "text",
            "text": "**Roster countries:** Yazaki — JPN, Sumitomo Electric — JPN, Aptiv — USA.\n\n**Same treatment:** Yazaki and Sumitomo Electric share a roster country (JPN), so on this field alone they'd be grouped together, with Aptiv (USA) separate.\n\n**What the roster country doesn't tell you:** it's a company/roster attribution, not a country of origin for the goods. It says nothing about where the harnesses are actually manufactured — wire harnesses from all three are commonly built in Mexico, Eastern Europe, North Africa or Southeast Asia. Duty depends on the origin of the shipped part (and rules like substantial transformation, USMCA content, tariff classification), none of which is in this data. So I can't tell you the actual duty exposure for any of them from the roster."
